# This data set was generated by a Navier Stoke flow solver I wrote more than 15 years ago. The simulation models 5 jets entering a rectangular region. Here are the first 2000 time steps of the simulation. While the flow modeled is neither complex nor very interesting, this data set would be good for conducting some fundamental study of time-varying visualization. 

# There are 5 variables in the data set: r (density), e (energy) and, x, y and z components of v (velocity).   The spatial resolution is 128x128x128 float (32 bits).  I can generate a higher resolution version of the data but space would become an issue. 

# You probably don't need every time step. Downloading every 10th time step will suffice for most of your studies. 

# If you have any question about this data set, feel free to contact me (ma@cs.ucdavis.edu). 

